<%- include("header") %>
<div class="column-form">
<% if (connection.demo) { %>
<h1>Your demo connection</h1>
<p class="callout"><strong>Copy the key now.</strong> It is shown only on this page. It stops working <%- include("time", { iso: connection.expires_at }) %>; you can get another from the welcome page.</p>
<p>Your assistant sees only the sample ticket made for assistants, as it was first written, and what it writes itself. It never receives what other visitors' assistants write, and theirs never receive what yours writes. On this demo everyone shares one team view, so anyone who views as Demo Team Member can see what your assistant wrote.</p>
<% } else { %>
<h1>Connection issued</h1>
<p class="callout"><strong>Copy the key now.</strong> It is shown only on this page. If it is lost, revoke the connection and issue a new one.</p>
<% } %>

<p class="can-read">It can read: <%= connection.demo ? "the sample ticket made for assistants" : "the tickets handed to it" %>, <%= connection.scopes.includes("read_notes") ? "with the team's internal notes" : "without internal notes" %>.</p>
<p>It may: <%= connection.scopes.map((s) => scopeLabels[s]).join("; ") %>.</p>

<label>
  Key for <span class="user-text"><%= connection.name %></span>
  <input type="text" readonly value="<%= key %>" class="key" />
</label>
<button type="button" class="copy secondary" data-copy="<%= key %>" hidden>Copy</button>

<h2>Connect Claude Code</h2>
<p>Paste this in a terminal:</p>
<% const claudeCode = `claude mcp add --transport http proofdesk ${address}/mcp --header "Authorization: Bearer ${key}"`; %>
<pre class="paste" id="claude-code"><code>claude mcp add --transport http proofdesk <%= address %>/mcp --header "Authorization: Bearer <%= key %>"</code></pre>
<button type="button" class="copy secondary" data-copy="<%= claudeCode %>" hidden>Copy</button>

<h2>Other assistants</h2>
<p>The MCP endpoint is <code><%= address %>/mcp</code>; send the key as <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;key&gt;</code>. In Claude Desktop, add a custom connector with that address and the key as a request header, where your organization has that option. An assistant that runs commands can also call the API directly:</p>
<% const curlCommand = `curl -H "Authorization: Bearer ${key}" "${address}/api/tickets?status=new"`; %>
<pre class="paste"><code>curl -H "Authorization: Bearer <%= key %>" "<%= address %>/api/tickets?status=new"</code></pre>
<button type="button" class="copy secondary" data-copy="<%= curlCommand %>" hidden>Copy</button>

<% if (connection.demo) { %>
<p><a href="/sign-in">Back to the welcome page</a></p>
<% } else { %>
<p><a href="/connections">Back to connections</a></p>
<% } %>
</div>
<%- include("footer") %>
